adjudication.rationale:
In the new API route `apps/web/pages/api/webhook/app-credential.ts`, the webhook secret check is implemented as a direct equality comparison:

```ts
if (
  req.headers[process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_HEADER_NAME || "calcom-webhook-secret"] !==
  process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET
) {
  return res.status(403).json({ message: "Invalid webhook secret" });
}
```

This uses `!==` on attacker-controlled input vs a server secret, which is not a constant-time comparison and can theoretically leak information via timing differences. A constant-time comparison (e.g., `crypto.timingSafeEqual` on normalized Buffers) is the standard mitigation for this kind of secret check. This issue is directly present in the diff and is a reasonable security finding.
